    stage_rows=['EEMMLL','MLLEEM','LMELME']
    review(747,'stable regional mosaic','D4.2','Two late patches at each survey give stable regional area shares because areas are equal. No patch remains late throughout. Snapshots permit recurrent change but cannot reconstruct all transitions; local succession and regional stability can coexist.','Rows are years and columns are individually aligned spatial patches; colours/key encode E/M/L states and no fixed regional climax is inferred.',[
        ('late count each survey',sum(row.count('L') for row in stage_rows)/3,2,'patches'),('late area fraction',2/6,1/3,'fraction'),('continuously late',sum(all(row[i]=='L' for row in stage_rows) for i in range(6)),0,'patches')],['1/3','No patch','snapshots'])
    review(748,'Small shifts in hatching','D4.3','Peak food demand follows hatching by7days. Prey advances15days but demand only3, increasing mismatch12days. Different temperature/photoperiod cues can decouple interacting species; an earlier date alone does not demonstrate genetic evolution.','All bars are day-of-year endpoints with demand distinct from hatch date; supplied values are constructed, not attributed to genuine great-tit field data.',[
        ('cool demand',135+7,142,'day of year'),('warm demand',132+7,139,'day of year'),('cool absolute mismatch',abs(142-140),2,'days'),('warm absolute mismatch',abs(139-125),14,'days'),('increase',14-2,12,'days'),('prey advance',140-125,15,'days')],['photoperiod','heritable'])
    review(749,'fractional generation','D4.3','Supplied threshold/no-carryover model requires flooring complete generations, so780degree-days gives2complete, not3. Multiplication applies only completed cycles. Real thermal variation, resources and mortality limit extrapolation to outbreaks.','X/Y/Z degree-day bars match stated temperature-duration inputs and do not label2.6 as3complete generations.',[
        ('X thermal sum',(15-10)*120,600,'°C days'),('Y thermal sum',(16.5-10)*120,780,'°C days'),('Z thermal sum',(18-10)*150,1200,'°C days'),('Y complete cycles',math.floor(780/300),2,'generations'),('Z complete cycles',math.floor(1200/300),4,'generations'),('Z/X multiplication',3**4/3**2,9,'ratio')],['two complete','four complete','mortality'])
    review(750,'Climate-related survival','D4.3','Morph frequencies use treatment-specific survivor denominators. Heritability and differential reproduction are needed for population evolution. Unknown dominance/locus structure prevents inserting brown phenotype proportion directly as q or q².','Expected snowy40/240 and low-snow90/225 survivor bars preserve matched starting cohorts; neither morph count is labeled an allele frequency.',[
        ('initial brown',100/400,.25,'morph fraction'),('snowy brown',(.4*100)/(.4*100+.8*300),1/7,'survivor morph fraction'),('low-snow brown',(.9*100)/(.9*100+.75*300),2/7,'survivor morph fraction')],['heritable','not automatically an allele frequency'])
    assert len(RECORDS)==50
    rawhash=hashlib.sha256(DATA.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
    assert rawhash=='e368ddcdcb7137b99f118b2008e03a0b87c143bf519c37832902ff939edabdbe','Reviewed canonical handoff changed.'
    result={'status':'passed','questions':50,'subject':'biology','theme':'D','sha256':rawhash,'numericalCheckCount':sum(len(r['numericalEvidence']) for r in RECORDS),'scopeSources':['https://xmltwo.ibo.org/publications/EAD/2026_EN/GR4/GR4-Biology_EN.pdf'],'method':'Independent full question/solution reading, fresh numerical reconstruction, statement-level scope and complete SVG visual review. Author generator is not imported.','visualReview':'Inspected all 50 final SVGs in five d-contact sheets. Explicitly rechecked revised 707 joined sister chromatids, 712 pedigree mating line, 718 separate biomass/oxygen panels, 727 cell-count labels, 733 near-wall incipient detachment, 740 rescaled marker load and 747 patch-column alignment.','resolvedFindings':['D718: algae and dissolved oxygen now use distinct panels with their own units.','D727: DNA-content measurements consistently refer to cells rather than isolated nuclei containing mitotic cells.','D733: incipient plasmolysis now shows near-wall detachment rather than advanced contraction.'],'limitations':'Independent AI review, not moderation by human IB examiners. Constructed practice evidence is not genuine published research.','records':RECORDS}
    if '--write-review' in sys.argv:
        REPORT.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
        REPORT.write_text(json.dumps(result,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n',encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
    else:
        old=json.loads(REPORT.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
        assert old['sha256']==rawhash,'Question JSON changed after review.'
        assert old['records']==result['records'],'Per-ID review record changed.'
    print(json.dumps({k:result[k] for k in ['status','questions','numericalCheckCount','sha256']}))

